 - `TripViewBeta` adds an Entrega column: only multi-item in-progress trips offer Entregar for undelivered linked commercial assets. `FiscalMercanciaItem.deliverd` supplies the Entregado marker on every trip size; canceled final movements use Movimiento finalizado. The delivery initializer of `ConfirmTripStatusUpdate` reuses one-item comments, local uploads, remote camera and gallery evidence, blocks confirmation during pending image uploads, and validates linked routes/unique safe filenames. The parent serializes status/delivery mutations and owns one popup, closes it on removal, checks session/trip/asset/snapshot response identities, then applies only the confirmed item flag and returned trip status (including auto-completion), notifies the dashboard/caller and refreshes trip/notes. Generation and confirmed-item checks reject stale refreshes. Optional destination section/subsection are omitted by this UI. App target compilation verified with the updated shared packages; browser/mobile/server behavior remains unverified.
 - In order mode, `TCOrderViewTheme` scopes the `AccoutOverview` shell to the standalone `SalePointView` holder geometry: top 25px, left 40px, width `calc(100% - 100px)`, height `calc(100% - 70px)` and 24px rounded corners. The theme retains its existing zero shell padding and border-box sizing. Internal OrderView elements, toolbar/content rules and corner speech icon placement are unchanged. Source-audited; browser rendering remains unverified.
 - `AssetItemView.dataColumn` edits the existing update contract fields: name, serial, current cost, section and subsection. Other item/custody metadata remains read-only and service-card activation stays separate. `Guardar Cambios` validates exact nonnegative cents and classification IDs, calls `updateAssettem` with the loaded item UUID, accepts a successful nil-note no-op response, and reloads authoritative details/notes by UUID. Current classification scope supplies catalog choices; failed catalog reads preserve existing IDs, and changing section clears its subsection. Mount/session/generation guards and disabled controls protect pending loads/saves. Source-audited; browser/build behavior remains unverified.
+- `AssetView` and `AssetItemView` notes reuse the account `QuickMessageObject` rows in compact bordered scroll containers, ordered newest first with alternating backgrounds, date/time, the note type description, resolved author and wrapped activity text. The full-note initializer preserves ID, timestamp, actor, type and activity while adapting to the existing display model; actorless full notes show Sistema. Asset rows disable priority-change actions through an optional flag whose existing-caller default remains enabled. Asset note data/counts and save/refresh paths remain intact. Source/diff reviewed; build and live rendering remain unverified.
 - Store configuration binds existing and newly created `StoreView` instances to `display: flex` when selected and `display: none` otherwise, preserving the theme’s bounded flex column so its card grid fills the available workspace height. `StoreView.usersContainers` retains `flex: 1 1 0`, an initial zero height, `min-height: 0`, and automatic overflow; the user list grows between its header and action and excess rows scroll. The supplied recording showed the prior block-display override leaving unused space below the cards. Loading and user-card interactions remain unchanged; source-audited, fixed browser rendering remains unverified.
 - `CustAssetsAvatarUploader` accepts an optional `[MediaViewer.MediaFile]` image list, initializes the current avatar first, and shows at most five 12px selection dots beneath the preview. Selecting a dot changes the preview without changing the saved avatar; clicking the preview opens the existing MediaViewer with the full photo list at that image and media actions disabled. Asset-item detail supplies its existing photos and displays only the uploader preview, with no separate thumbnail grid below it. Its marked `isAvatar` photo uses the saved item avatar as its preview reference while retaining the original file/ID. Avatar matching and upload reconciliation compare image identities with recognized thump_/og_/wap_ prefixes and query/fragment suffixes removed, preserving host/directory identity and all render URLs; a matching photo is reused instead of adding a duplicate standalone avatar. Upload results and external avatar changes restore focus to the current avatar. Updated on 2026-10-14; source review only, browser/build behavior remains unverified.
 - `ManageLocationItem` exposes a bottom-left red crystal Eliminar action for an existing editor ID linked to a saved `.location` source. It uses the linked `locationId`, not the generated editor UUID, with the existing `deleteLocation` confirmation/error flow. The endpoint cancels the saved location without deleting its database record. Only success closes the editor and notifies `CreateTripView` through its existing saved-location list/selection cleanup; pending deletion prevents duplicate calls and saving. An optional live deletion-policy closure defaults to allowing deletion; trip creation denies deletion of its primary stops while additional destinations exist and rechecks before confirmation submission. The existing `removeLocation` trip-stop operation is not called. Browser/server behavior remains unverified.
